            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0215" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.4215 Air Pollution/84: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Canada</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Newson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-07T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 7,
                                1928—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>108. Your 171, August 4, 1 p.m. By letter dated today<anchor n="65"
                        xml:id="d56-f1"/> Department submitting Trail Smelter matter to
                    International Joint Commission in accordance with agreement.</p>
                <p>Please express to Canadian Government this Government’s appreciation of its
                    cooperation in this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
